response.summary:
VERDICT: APPROVED. The revised plan resolves C1-C4 and the earlier F1-F9 dispositions. I found no material unresolved defects in the specification. This is an approval of the plan only. No implementation, render or test has been inspected, and the host says final code gets a fresh inspection.

RESOLUTION CHECK
- C1 (zone): resolved. The spec uses the validated agenda.data.time_zone, falls back to the device zone, derives day keys with Intl in that zone, and keeps date-only values as plain calendar dates. That matches the server, which buckets by calendar.timeZone (desk.ts:156-157, 246) and sends all-day events as date-only strings (desk.ts:218-219).
- C2 (false zero on truncated lists): resolved. Counts are 'upcoming event starts' qualified as loaded. Absence reads 'no upcoming starts loaded' whenever the data is incomplete or stale (next_cursor set, with max 20 events per desk.ts:168, 231-240). The full-calendar link is retained, and setup, loading and error are never equated to zero. No extra backend call is needed.
- C3 (window shape): resolved. The 7-day column set is anchored to fetched_at, today is partial, and the 8th day is excluded. This matches a window that starts at fetched_at and ends seven calendar days later. Counting starts only avoids claiming spanning events as whole-day availability.
- C4: resolved. Default selection is today and persists by date key with a fallback to today, buttons are single-select with aria-pressed and full date-and-count names, the scroll region is keyboard-focusable, and teacher-only class names avoid the student .classroom-home-day selectors.
- Height rule: accepting natural content growth and rejecting fixed empty-to-populated height is consistent with the compact empty-state goal. It supersedes my earlier stable-height remark, and I do not dispute it.

SCORE
- Unchanged: 51 of 95 assessed, motion 5 points unassessed (not a defect), accessibility partial. No new render was inspected, so there is no re-score.

FINAL RECOMMENDATION
Proceed with the teacher-scoped implementation under the stated gates:
- zone-vs-device, DST spring and fall, date-only, partial-cursor, selection-fallback and day-boundary tests;
- all ready-empty, loading, setup, error and populated branches;
- 320, 390, 683, 1024 and 1440 widths and the docked view, with no page overflow at 320;
- keyboard walk-through, the menu, and normal and reduced-motion playback;
- measured contrast on actual surface tokens;
- student Home, routes, read state and permissions unchanged;
- typecheck, build and affected tests.

Benefit: a distinctive, truthful week strip and calmer composition. Risks: shared-style leakage and count wording drift. Both are covered by the gates.
